**DAY 3 SUBMISSION**

Product Performance & Inventory Analysis — Project Report

**Project:** Product_Performance_Analysis
**GitHub Link:** https://github.com/natnaelaster/Daily-exercise/tree/main/day_3_product_performance & enventory Avalysis
**Tableau Link:** https://public.tableau.com/app/profile/natnael.birhanu/viz/productperformanceanalysis_17625987423580/Dashboard2

Executive summary
Five years of transaction data were analyzed to produce product-level KPIs, time‑series exports and inventory estimates to support replenishment, promotions and SKU rationalization. Outputs available for operational use: product_performance_file.csv, product_performance_enriched.csv, monthly_trend.csv and related exports.

Methods (brief)

Aggregated sales by StockCode/Description to compute Total Revenue and Units Sold.
Derived Sales Velocity = Units Sold / Days Active (First → Last sale).
Where cost data exists, computed Profit and Profit Margin.
Built monthly time series per SKU for turnover, seasonality and trend analysis.
Estimated safety stock, lead‑time demand, reorder point and EOQ from monthly stats (configurable lead time & service level).
Flagged stockout risk using coefficient of variation (CV) of monthly demand; identified declining SKUs by comparing last 3 months vs previous 3 months.
Key results

Revenue & units
Total Revenue and Units Sold computed per SKU (see product_performance_enriched.csv).
Profit margin available when Cost is present in source data.
Top / Bottom performers
Top 10 SKUs by revenue exported (top_10_products_by_revenue.csv).
Bottom 10 positive‑revenue SKUs exported (bottom_10_products_by_revenue.csv).
Small set of SKUs drives a large share of revenue (ABC effect; top ~20% ≈ 80% of revenue).
Sales velocity & movement
Sales_velocity computed (units/day) and SKUs bucketed into Slow / Medium / Fast movement for differentiated replenishment rules.
Inventory analysis
Inventory turnover (units-based) estimated where OnHand exists: AnnualUnits / AvgOnHand (inventory_turnover_by_product.csv).
SafetyStock and ReorderPoint computed from AvgDailySales and demand volatility; EOQ included when cost parameters supplied (inventory_estimates_by_product.csv).
Stockout risk
3‑tier stockout_risk flags generated from CV of monthly demand (low / medium / high) — high CV SKUs need safety stock/shorter review cycles (stockout_risk_by_product.csv).
Seasonality & trends
Seasonality score (low/medium/high) from monthly std; 8 categories show clear seasonal patterns (seasonal_products.csv).
12 SKUs identified as Decline by 3‑month vs prior 3‑month comparison (declining_products.csv).
monthly_trend.csv contains the monthly series for forecasting and visualization.
Operational implications

Prioritize replenishment and lead‑time reduction for fast movers and Top‑A SKUs to avoid lost sales.
Increase safety stock or shorten review cycles for high CV SKUs (stockout risk).
Run 4–8 week promotional tests on declining SKUs; consider bundling/liquidation if no recovery.
Use movement buckets to set review cadence: Fast = daily/weekly, Medium = weekly, Slow = monthly/quarterly.
Align procurement calendar with seasonal SKU peaks.
